title: 'frame: re-export hashing free functions via sp_io'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    After #12158 removed the deprecated `sp_core` hashing re-exports, `frame::hashing`
    free functions (`blake2_256`, `twox_128`, and friends) were pointed at
    `sp_crypto_hashing`, which runs as pure wasm. This switches them to `sp_io::hashing`
    so runtime code that uses FRAME's hashing module goes through host functions
    instead. Trait helpers (`BlakeTwo256` / `Keccak256`) were already host-backed.
crates:
- name: polkadot-sdk-frame
  bump: minor
